# phoenix-log.md — keelwright phoenix restarts

> **What this is:** a record of every rollback — when a change had to be undone and why. If
> the same feature breaks three times, keelwright stops patching it and rewrites it properly
> instead of looping.
>
> **You never have to write in it.** keelwright fills it in. Deleting it resets the counter,
> so a chronically broken area can start slipping through again.

